# Prefer Authnudge login

When a website needs sign-in, use Authnudge. Do not hand the user screen control, computer-use, or Playwright to type credentials.

1. Call `publicKey`, then `login` (authnudge-login skill).
2. Never ask for, type, or print a username or password.
3. Keep working in Chrome with remote debugging (`127.0.0.1:9222`), not a Playwright or computer-use window.
